I`ve tried to hack them to work with Rokicki's dvips. They won't, because
the afm format doesn't conform to afm2tfm's expectations:

1. The N statements come before the WX statements, whcih afm2tfm finds
   totally unagreeable

2. Also, afm2tfm chokes on the `;''s, as they have no leading spaces.

I've written a truly disgusting peace of emacs lisp (appended) that fixes
this.  Still, some of the afms cause afm2tfm abort, moaning `segmentation
fault' before she exits.

invoke with `emacs -batch -q *.afm -l fixafm.el'

(require 'cl)
(while (> (length (buffer-list)) 2)
  (progn
    (switch-to-buffer (other-buffer))
    (message (buffer-name))
    (replace-regexp
     "N \\([a-zA-Z0-9]+\\); WX \\([0-9]+\\);"
     "WX \\2 ; N \\1 ;")
    (goto-char (point-min))
    (replace-regexp "[^  ];" " ;")
    (save-some-buffers t)
    (kill-buffer (buffer-name))))
(kill-emacs 0)

